# virtualisation in the cloud

hypervisor : piece of hardware or software that creates and run vm machine 
 - allow multiple os to run on a single machine
 - refered as host computer and vm are guest 
 - responsible for managing resources for guest OS
 - 2 types:  type 1 hypervisor created and deployed on a bare metal installation             
             act as a os for a bare metal machine 
             communicate directly with hardware and boots befor os 

             type2 hypervisor loaded on top of an already existing os installation
                             relies o the os 




